      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ellsworth sprang from a coal boom when James Ellsworth built a shaft mine and coke yard in 1900, later selling the mines to Bethlehem Steel in the 1920s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellsworth%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bethlehem Mines kept mining at Ellsworth until 1982, making it one of the longest‑running coal operations in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://coalcampusa.com/westpa/pittsburgh/ellsworth/ellsworth.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ellsworth’s brick “coal patch” houses stand out because they are single‑family structures, unlike the common two‑family miner homes elsewhere.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
